# PART A — FRONTEND (build first, against mocks)

## Phase 0 – Frontend Scaffolding & Design System

**Goal:** A runnable React/Vite app with routing, a component/design-token baseline, and state-management conventions established, containing no real feature screens yet.

**Tasks:**
- Scaffold a React + Vite project (TypeScript). Set up routing (React Router) with placeholder routes for: `/login`, `/register`, `/verify-email`, `/reset-password`, `/dashboard`, `/certificates/new`, `/certificates/:id`, `/verify/:certId` (public), `/verify` (public, blank form).
- **Establish the design-token file as the single source of truth for color, spacing, and typography** (e.g., a Tailwind theme config or CSS variables file) per the UI Development Standards above. Do not default to an assumed palette — if no brand colors/reference are supplied, ask one clarifying question to establish a minimal palette: primary, a neutral gray scale, and semantic `success`/`warning`/`danger`/`info` colors. Explicitly define the color **and** icon/label pairing for each of the five certificate statuses (`PENDING`/`VALID`/`EXPIRED`/`REVOKED`/`FAILED`) and four verification outcomes here, once, so no later phase has to invent them.
- Build the shared component set (Button, Input, Card, Badge/StatusPill, Table, Modal, Toast) sourcing every color/spacing/type value from the token file — zero raw hex values or arbitrary utility classes anywhere in these components.
- Build one shared authenticated-page layout wrapper and one shared public-page layout wrapper (header/nav placement, content max-width, padding rhythm), per the layout-consistency rule, for later phases to use rather than each defining their own page shell.
- Set up a global state/data-fetching convention (e.g., TanStack Query or a lightweight context) that all later phases will use to call the (currently mock) API layer, so swapping mocks for real calls in Part B is a one-line change per hook, not a rewrite.
- Set up an `.env`-based config for `VITE_API_BASE_URL`, defaulted to a value the mock layer will intercept.

**SRS Requirements Addressed:** §4.1 (User Interfaces, scaffolding only)
**Phase Completion Criteria:**
- `npm run dev` serves the app with all placeholder routes reachable and rendering a "Coming soon" stub.
- Shared component set is used by at least one placeholder screen (proves the imports work, not just that files exist).
- A repo-wide search for raw hex values (`#[0-9a-fA-F]{3,6}`) and inline `style={{color:`/`rgb(` usage outside the token file returns zero matches.
- The five certificate statuses and four verification outcomes each have a defined color, icon, and label in the token/component layer, listed in one place for later phases to reference.
- Two page-shell components exist (authenticated, public) and no screen-specific layout code exists yet, since no feature screens have been built.

