## Phase 4 – Organization Dashboard UI (Frontend, Mocked)

**Goal:** Authenticated users can list, search, and view certificate details against the mock data, with all five statuses rendered distinctly.

**Tasks:**
- Build `/dashboard`: a paginated, searchable/filterable table of certificates (recipient name, Certificate ID, issue date, status badge), per FR-3.1/3.2/NFR-2.2. Use the shared `Table` and `StatusPill` components from Phase 0.
- Build `/certificates/:id`: full detail view including the blockchain transaction reference field (rendered as a stub/placeholder value from the mock until Part B provides a real one), per FR-3.3.
- Build the "stale PENDING" and `FAILED` states as visibly actionable (a "Retry Issuance" button, disabled/wired to a mock endpoint) per FR-2.9, so the UI affordance exists before the backend logic behind it does.
- Add pagination controls wired to the mock's paginated response shape.

**SRS Requirements Addressed:** FR-3.1–3.3, NFR-2.2 (frontend rendering; organization-scoping enforcement is a backend concern, Part B)
**Phase Completion Criteria:**
- Dashboard table renders all fixture certificates with correct status badges for each of the five statuses.
- Search/filter narrows the visible rows against the mock data without a full page reload.
- Clicking into a certificate shows its full detail view, including a visible (even if placeholder) blockchain reference.
- A `FAILED` and a stale-`PENDING` fixture both show a "Retry Issuance" action.
- Pagination controls change the visible page against a mock dataset large enough to require more than one page (extend Phase 1 fixtures if needed).
- **UI Standards check:** status badges in the table and detail view use the exact same `StatusPill` component and Phase 0 status/color/icon definitions (no re-implementation); the dashboard and detail screens use the shared authenticated-page layout wrapper.

