## Phase 6 – Frontend Polish, UI Standards Audit & State-Coverage Review

**Goal:** Close remaining UX gaps and formally audit the whole frontend against the UI Development Standards before backend work begins, so Part B is purely "wire it up," not "also finish or clean up the UI."

**Tasks:**
- Review every screen from Phases 2–5 against a checklist of states: loading, empty, error, and each relevant status value — fill any gaps found.
- Add responsive/mobile layout passes for the public verification page and the dashboard table (these are the two screens most likely to be used on a phone, per SRS §4.2's QR-scanning context).
- Add basic accessibility passes (form labels, focus management on modals, color contrast for status badges) since status color-coding (FR-5.6's tamper warning, FR-4.3's five statuses) currently carries meaning primarily through color.
- Confirm the mock service layer can be disabled via a single config flag (`VITE_API_BASE_URL` pointing at a real backend) without any component code changes — this is the actual test of whether Phase 1's contract discipline held.
- **Run a full UI Development Standards audit** across the entire codebase built so far:
  - Grep for raw hex/RGB values and arbitrary color utility classes outside the token file — fix every hit.
  - Diff every "Button," "Input," "Card," "Modal," etc. instance across all screens for structural near-duplication (>80% identical markup); consolidate any found.
  - Confirm every status/outcome badge across all three screens (dashboard, detail, public verification) resolves to the exact same token definitions from Phase 0 — not per-screen re-implementations that happen to look similar.
  - Confirm every screen uses one of the two shared page-shell layouts from Phase 0 — no screen-specific layout code.

**SRS Requirements Addressed:** §5.3 (Usability)
**Phase Completion Criteria:**
- A written checklist (loading/empty/error/each-status) is completed for every screen built in Phases 2–5, with no unchecked gaps.
- Public verification and dashboard screens are usable at a mobile viewport width (test at 375px).
- Status badges are distinguishable by shape/icon/text, not color alone.
- Flipping `VITE_API_BASE_URL` and disabling the mock layer changes zero component source files (only config).
- **UI Standards audit results are documented with zero unresolved findings**: zero raw color values outside the token file, zero unresolved near-duplicate components, zero screen-specific layout shells, and a confirmed single definition source for every status/outcome badge used anywhere in the app.

